<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>WW3 D-Day. 1985</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;NATO vs. USSR&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Date/Time: June 6th, 1985 / 05:00:00&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Location: Normandy, France&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Playable Side: NATO&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;U&gt;Background&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The second term of President Reagan was going to start as the first one had ended, with NATO, with the United States at the front, leading a winning crusade against socialism. Increasing voices of dissent were growing in the oppressed countries of Poland, the Baltic States and Hungary, and more people were crossing illegally in Berlin.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Soviet Central Committee has conceived a plan to turn the tide and start winning the conventional Cold War. In the early days of May, Soviet armored columns crossed the West-East Germany Border while precise artillery fire knocked out NATO positions. The precise employment of Spetznaz agents, cyber attacks and conventional strikes have rendered NATO's nuclear response useless, and the counter strike that followed also deemed ineffective Russia's nuclear deterrent.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;So, with a conventional war in their hands, the NATO allies find themselves pushed back all the way to the Atlantic coast. There, as if it was 40 years ago, the Western counter strike shall begin...&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is a onesided scenaro that combines ASW, ASuW (Naval &amp;amp; Surface) and AAW. It has a duration of 60h (2d 12h).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;v1.0&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
